This licence covers the code in code/, js/, qa_live/ and reddit/ and the page scripts.
The text of the page, the paper and blog post in release/, the figures, the
glyph drawings and the derived files in data/ are released under CC BY 4.0.
The repository holds no OpenStreetMap tile data; the map reads it live.

Third-party material:
- Map renders (figures, header.png, the Reddit poster) contain OpenStreetMap
  data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence 1.0, served by
  OpenFreeMap in the OpenMapTiles schema (c) OpenMapTiles.
- Elevation: AWS Terrain Tiles (Mapzen and its sources: SRTM, GMTED2010,
  ETOPO1 and others); see their attribution notes.
- data/labels_countries.geojson is derived from Natural Earth (public domain)
  and ONS Local Authority District boundaries (Open Government Licence v3.0,
  contains OS data (c) Crown copyright and database right 2023).
- data/gazetteer.json is derived from Natural Earth (public domain).
- data/heritage/, data/hills/, data/landmarks.geojson and data/peaks_famous.geojson
  are derived from Wikidata (CC0). data/rivers.geojson and data/lakes.geojson
  are derived from Natural Earth (public domain). data/walls.geojson is derived from OpenStreetMap
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence 1.0, and is made
  available under that licence. Ship positions in data/decor.geojson follow
  passages from the CLIWOC logbook database (1750 to 1850). The same holds for
  data/walls_major.geojson, data/walls_boxes.json and data/grid/walls/ (cut from
  walls.geojson) and data/forts*.geojson and data/grid/forts/ (OpenStreetMap, ODbL).
- data/life/: data/life/roman_roads/ is derived from Itiner-e (CC BY 4.0);
  data/life/pilgrim_routes/ from OpenStreetMap (ODbL 1.0, available under that
  licence); data/life/battles/, wrecks/ and monasteries/ from Wikidata (CC0);
  data/life/lost_villages/ from Beresford's Lost Villages (University of Hull),
  CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, and Wikidata (CC0), and is made available under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0.
- fonts/ttf/ holds MedievalSharp and IM Fell fonts under the SIL Open Font
  License 1.1 (licence texts alongside). fonts/Ink */ are SDF glyph sets
  generated from them (a modified version, so they carry new names and do not
  use the reserved font name), under the same licence.
